   m_sSRZReadText "Gravitational fields. Fields G-2 and G-5. Leaves and dust circle in the air above them. Small ones throw you. Large ones pull you in and do not let go, the spinning type we call the whirligig. Nothing that went into the centre of a whirligig came out in one piece. The bolt test works, but watch where the bolt lands. It shows you the edge, not the centre."
